#!/usr/bin/env python3

"""
Smoke-test the treetime CLI and compare its outputs with a baseline snapshot.

dev/smoke runs the treetime CLI over a matrix of commands, datasets and flag variants. The outputs of
each run go into a snapshot directory named after the git state that built the binary. The current
snapshot is then compared with a baseline snapshot, by default the one of the `rust` branch. The
script reports crashes, timeouts, missing outputs and changed outputs, with the command, stderr and
the changed values of each case.

The cases are defined in dev/smoke.toml: one row per command variant, with its flags, the datasets it
runs on and its expected failures. The header of that file documents every field. `--overview` prints
what the file produces.

Run it on the host. It needs git and Docker: the binaries are built with `./dev/docker/run just br
treetime`, and the cases run inside the container.

Usage:

    ./dev/smoke                           quick tier, compared with `rust`
    ./dev/smoke --tier full               every case
    ./dev/smoke --against <ref-or-id>     compare with another commit, branch or snapshot
    ./dev/smoke --no-compare              statuses only, no baseline build
    ./dev/smoke --only <regex>            cases whose id matches the regex
    ./dev/smoke --rerun-failed            cases that did not pass in the last run
    ./dev/smoke --list                    print the selected case ids

Options:

    --tier quick|full       quick (default): datasets of at most 100 sequences, help cases and a few
                            larger timetree cases. full: every case
    --only REGEX            select the cases whose id matches REGEX (re.search)
    --rerun-failed          select the cases that did not pass in the last run of the current snapshot,
                            or, when it has no run yet, in the most recent run of any snapshot
    --list                  print the selected case ids and exit
    --overview              print the selected cases per command and variant, with their datasets, and exit
    --against REF_OR_ID     baseline: an existing snapshot id, or a git ref (default: rust)
    --no-compare            run the current snapshot only and report statuses
    --jobs N                number of cases that run at the same time (default: CPU count)
    --timeout-scale X       multiply every case timeout by X
    --memory-budget GIB     memory the running cases may use together (default: 75% of the memory available at
                            start). Each case reserves the largest peak of its earlier completed runs plus 25%, or
                            2 GiB (at most 100 sequences) and 8 GiB (at most 500) when never measured; a larger
                            case without a completed run runs alone. Every treetime process is limited to the
                            budget, so a case that needs more fails with an allocation error
    --rerun                 run the selected cases again even when stored results are reusable
    --no-build              use the existing .out/treetime for the current snapshot
    --check-determinism     run each selected case a second time with `treetime --jobs=1` and mark
                            the case nondeterministic when the outputs differ
    --prune                 delete the dirty snapshots other than the current one, then exit

Snapshots (git-ignored, at the repository root):

    snapshots/<id>/                 <id> = short commit, or <short-commit>+dirty-<hash> for a
                                    working tree with uncommitted or untracked changes
      snapshot.json                 commit, dirty hash, ref, binary SHA-256, creation time
      bin/treetime                  the binary that produced the snapshot
      last-run.json                 statuses of the last run (for --rerun-failed)
      cases/<case-id>/
        out/                        raw outputs, never modified
        stdout.txt, stderr.txt
        cmd.sh                      the exact command, runnable from the repository root in the container
        result.json                 status, exit code, wall and CPU time, case key
        rerun/                      second run of --check-determinism
      compare/<baseline-id>/        report.tsv and report.md of a comparison
      report.tsv, report.md         report of a --no-compare run

A stored case is reused when its case key (argv, expectation, declared outputs, working directory and
the SHA-256 of every input file) is unchanged and its result is consistent with the requested timeout.
A snapshot whose binary changed loses its stored cases. Clean-commit snapshots stay until deleted by
hand; the git ref baseline is built in a temporary worktree under tmp/smoke/worktrees/.

Case statuses:

    ok                  exit code 0 and every declared output is present and non-empty
    failed              non-zero exit code, or an expected failure that failed differently
    missing-output      exit code 0, but a declared output is missing or empty
    timeout             the case exceeded its timeout
    xfail               the case failed or timed out as declared in the matrix
    xpass               a case declared to fail passed: remove the expectation
    nondeterministic    the --check-determinism rerun produced different outputs

Comparison categories (current against baseline):

    identical           both passed and the outputs are equal            (pass)
    fixed               current passed, baseline did not; not compared   (pass)
    expected-failure    current is xfail                                 (pass)
    changed             both passed and the outputs differ               (fail)
    regressed           baseline passed, current did not                 (fail)
    still-failing       both did not pass, without an expectation       (fail)
    unexpected-pass     current is xpass                                 (fail)

Outputs are compared byte for byte, after removing `meta.updated` from `*.auspice.json` and
`generated_by.version` from `*.augur-node-data.json`. Numeric differences are summarized in the report,
never tolerated.

Exit codes:

    0   every selected case passed
    1   a case failed or changed
    2   the script could not complete (build failure, git error, invalid arguments, container failure)

Environment:

    SMOKE_WRAPPER       container wrapper command (default: ./dev/docker/run); empty runs in place
"""

